ries, usually written under the pen name Captain W. E. Johns. He is best remembered as the creator of the ace pilot and adventurer Biggles.\"}, {\"node_id\": \"detective\", \"kind\": \"implicit\", \"stance\": \"contradiction\", \"claim\": \"The fictional private detective that appears in \\\"The Adventure of the Seven Clocks\\\" is a character created by John le Carré.\", \"entity_scope\": \"The Adventure of the Seven Clocks\", \"event_time\": null, \"reason\": \"The source discusses John le Carré as an author of espionage novels, but there is no mention of 'The Adventure of the Seven Clocks' or any connection between this story and le Carré. Le Carré is known for spy fiction, not private detective stories.\", \"source_ids\": [\"src_0262124d24a5e05f1ae160de\"], \"time_source_ids\": [], \"doc_id\": \"hotpotqa:1471\", \"id\": \"e20\", \"assessment_id\": \"ev_2a731f8f3d7b6aeb29338ca6\", \"fragments\": [{\"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"premise_group_ids\": [\"prem_0a5128d2998d0c9a292d6a3f\", \"prem_b22619e54fd8f6790b710ecb\", \"prem_7520b382d94d091c4986830b\"], \"source_alias\": \"s34\", \"id\": \"src_0262124d24a5e05f1ae160de\", \"doc_id\": \"hotpotqa:1471\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 301, \"exact_quote\": \"John le Carré\\nDavid John Moore Cornwell (born 19 October 1931), known by the pseudonym John le Carré ( ), is a British author of espionage novels. During the 1950s and the 1960s, he worked for both the Security Service and the Secret Intelligence Service, and began writing novels under his pen name. \", \"raw_text_hash\": \"6a6585dd0d6980628e11954c083005ee082cb543a789a642c455526c57fd406a\", \"event_time\": null}], \"node_ids\": [\"detective\"], \"raw_text_hash\": \"6a6585dd0d6980628e11954c083005ee082cb543a789a642c455526c57fd406a\", \"source_role\": \"document\", \"source_message_indices\": [], \"premise_group_ids\": [\"prem_0a5128d2998d0c9a292d6a3f\", \"prem_7520b382d94d091c4986830b\", \"prem_b22619e54fd8f6790b710ecb\"], \"time_fragme